==English==
[[Image:Earthenware pottery for sale 2007.jpg|thumb|Earthenware pottery]]

===Etymology===
The first recorded appearance in 1673.<ref>''Chambers Dictionary of Etymology'', Robert K. Barnhart (ed.), Chambers, 1988</ref> Compound of [[earthen]] and [[ware]].

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|s|-}}

# An opaque, semi-porous [[ceramic]] made from clay and other compounds.

